# vim: set filetype=game:
# game: libninja
#
# name says which project this is. your game config has a block for it
# that says where its road and dist are; this file never names a remote.
name libninja

# lint rules for this repository. any lint line in a .game replaces all
# the lint rules in your game config, so these lines copy all of them.
# the last line is the one change: README.md may run past 25 rows,
# since it gives every scroll its reason.
lint width 80
lint rows 25
lint comments
lint print
lint exclaim
lint shout
lint words hyperscaler enterprise-grade blazing-fast load-bearing
lint paragraph 4
lint allow README.md rows

# the sweep refuses this machine's paths in a file. buried.go's work is
# to know what one looks like, so it holds the roots of such paths as
# patterns, not as places; it may carry them.
sweep allow buried.go paths
